{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.colourWeighted_target_forces_delta_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.colourWeighted_target_forces_delta_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypeWeightedChainRatio.lean#L183-L192","doc":"**Reaching the measured `b₃/b₂` would need `δ > 1`.** Solving\n`(4 - δ)/(2 - δ) = 3 + rMeasured` gives `δ = 4867718/3916903 ≈ 1.2427` — and\n`δ = (m_n - m_p)/M_N > 1` would need the neutron-proton mass difference to exceed\nthe whole nucleon mass. The physical value is `≈ 0.0013757`, so the required\nfigure is **903× too large and unphysical besides**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.colourWeighted_ratio_middleHeavy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.colourWeighted_ratio_middleHeavy","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypeWeightedChainRatio.lean#L172-L181","doc":"**The `middle-heavy` ratio under colour weighting is `(4 - δ)/(2 - δ)`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.colourWeighted_on_locus_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.colourWeighted_on_locus_iff","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypeWeightedChainRatio.lean#L163-L170","doc":"On the locus exactly when `δ = 0` — and `δ` is a nucleon mass-difference\nratio, so it is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.colourWeighted_off_locus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.colourWeighted_off_locus","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypeWeightedChainRatio.lean#L156-L161","doc":"**The colour-weighted interface sits OFF the arithmetic-mean locus, by exactly\n`δ/2`.** So the preceding theorems do not cover it — which is why it needed its\nown treatment rather than a remark. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.wpnColour","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.wpnColour","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypeWeightedChainRatio.lean#L151-L154","doc":"`d_for_ctype \"averaged_weighted\"` is `-h(1/2 - δ/4)`, with `δ` the substrate\nflavour split `(m_n - m_p)/M_N`. In units of `h`, that is the `pn` weight below;\n`pp` and `nn` are untouched by the colour weighting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.allPn_ratio_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.allPn_ratio_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypeWeightedChainRatio.lean#L140-L149","doc":"**An all-`pn` chain gives ratio `2` for ANY `pn` weight, with no locus\ncondition at all.** The `middle-light` arrangement (`n-p-n` and `p-n-p`) has only\n`pn` bonds, so the weight cancels entirely between numerator and denominator.\n\nThis is the sharpest form of the obstruction: on that arrangement `b₃/b₂ = -1`\n*whatever* the `pn` interface is — colour-weighted, `δ`-dependent, anything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.production_bRatio_eq_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.production_bRatio_eq_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypeWeightedChainRatio.lean#L133-L136","doc":"So production's type-weighted chain gives exactly `-1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.production_weights_on_mean_locus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.production_weights_on_mean_locus","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypeWeightedChainRatio.lean#L128-L131","doc":"Production's own weights, in units of `h`: `pp = 0`, `pn = -1/2`, `nn = -1`\n(`d_for_ctype`). They sit on the locus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.bRatio_eq_neg_one_of_mean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.bRatio_eq_neg_one_of_mean","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypeWeightedChainRatio.lean#L120-L126","doc":"**Hence `b₃/b₂ = -1` for every type weighting on the mean locus** — the same\nvalue the uniform chain gives, against a measured `+0.6411239316`. Weighting by\ntype is not an escape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.ratio_eq_two_of_mean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.ratio_eq_two_of_mean","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypeWeightedChainRatio.lean#L112-L118","doc":"**On that locus the triple/pair ratio is `2`, identically.** No dependence on\nthe weights, and none on `h` — so no anchor or convention can move it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.avgTriple_order_independent_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.avgTriple_order_independent_iff","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypeWeightedChainRatio.lean#L99-L110","doc":"**The isospin average is arrangement-independent exactly on the\narithmetic-mean locus.** Per isotope the chain does depend on which nucleon is in\nthe middle; averaging `³H` against `³He` cancels that iff `w_pp + w_nn = 2w_pn`.\nProduction satisfies it exactly (`0`, `-h/2`, `-h`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.muTripleMiddleLight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.muTripleMiddleLight","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypeWeightedChainRatio.lean#L95-L97","doc":"`A = 3` chain multiplicity with the *like* pair split — `³H` as `n-p-n` gives\n`{pn, pn}`, `³He` as `p-n-p` gives `{pn, pn}` — isospin averaged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.muTripleMiddleHeavy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.muTripleMiddleHeavy","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypeWeightedChainRatio.lean#L90-L93","doc":"`A = 3` chain multiplicity with the heavier-unlike nucleon at an end —\n`³H` as `p-n-n` gives `{pn, nn}`, `³He` as `p-p-n` gives `{pp, pn}` — isospin\naveraged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.muPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypeWeightedChainRatio.muPair","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypeWeightedChainRatio.lean#L87-L88","doc":"The chain multiplicity of `²H`: one `pn` bond. ","signatureChunk":0}]}